  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A current-carrying copper wire experiences a force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> when placed in a magnetic field of strength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B_{1}\"></span>. The length of the wire is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span>, the current in the wire is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> and the angle between the direction of the current and the direction of the magnetic field is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"90^{\\circ}\"></span>. When a similar copper wire of length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4L\"></span> carrying a current of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2I\"></span> is placed in a different magnetic field with strength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B_{2}\"></span>, it experiences a force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{2}\"></span>. The angle between the direction of the current and the direction of the magnetic field for this second wire is  also <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"90^{\\circ}\"></span>. What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{B_{1}}{B_{2}}\"></span>?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"16\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
